---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const downloadHref = '/downloads/anonymail-beta.zip';
const betaVersion = 'v0.1.0';
---
<BaseLayout title="Anonymail — a quiet disposable inbox for Chrome" description="Create one disposable inbox, fill signup forms, and read verification mail without leaving the page.">
  <header class="site-header wrap">
    <a class="logo" href="/" aria-label="Anonymail home"><img src="/anonymail.png" alt="" /><span>Anonymail</span></a>
    <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#how">How it works</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a class="nav-cta" href={downloadHref} download>Download latest beta</a></nav>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="hero wrap">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="kicker"><span></span> Free privacy beta for Chrome</p>
        <h1>A disposable inbox that stays beside you.</h1>
        <p class="hero-body">Right-click a signup field. Anonymail creates a private address, generates a different password, fills the form, and keeps verification mail in a calm side panel.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="button primary" href={downloadHref} download>Download latest beta</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="#install">See installation steps</a>
        </div>
        <div class="beta-bar" aria-label={`Latest beta ${betaVersion}`}>
          <span>Latest beta</span>
          <b>{betaVersion}</b>
          <a href={downloadHref} download>Developer Mode ZIP</a>
        </div>
        <p class="microcopy">No account · No analytics · One active inbox</p>
      </div>

      <div class="product-stage" aria-label="Anonymail dashboard preview">
        <div class="demo-shell">
          <aside class="demo-nav">
            <img src="/anonymail.png" alt="" />
            <div class="demo-nav-item active">Inbox <b>2</b></div>
            <div class="demo-nav-item">Settings</div>
            <div class="demo-nav-item">Privacy</div>
            <p>One quiet inbox.<br />No tracking.</p>
          </aside>
          <div class="demo-main">
            <div class="demo-address"><small>ACTIVE DISPOSABLE ADDRESS</small><strong>a2bcde@x.test</strong><span>52m 14s remaining</span></div>
            <div class="demo-inbox">
              <div class="demo-title">Inbox <span>2</span></div>
              <div class="demo-row unread"><i></i><b>Acme</b><span>Confirm your email</span><time>Now</time></div>
              <div class="demo-row selected"><i>✓</i><b>Studio</b><span>Your verification code: 482901</span><time>1m</time></div>
              <div class="demo-row"><i>✓</i><b>Newsletter</b><span>Welcome aboard</span><time>3m</time></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="trust-strip"><div class="wrap"><span>Explicit website access</span><span>Separate mailbox and signup secrets</span><span>Automatic expiry</span><span>Powered by Mail.tm</span></div></section>

    <section id="how" class="section wrap">
      <p class="kicker"><span></span> A smaller privacy ritual</p>
      <div class="section-heading"><h2>From signup to verification without changing context.</h2><p>Anonymail stays intentionally narrow: one inbox, one clear action, and no permanent access to every site you visit.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article>
          <video src="/media/right-click-fill.mp4" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" aria-label="Right-clicking a signup field and choosing Fill with Anonymail"></video>
          <div><b>Right-click fill</b><p>Access begins only after your explicit action. Anonymail fills the enabled signup fields locally.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <video src="/media/side-panel-or-tab.mp4" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" aria-label="Anonymail inbox open in Chrome’s side panel"></video>
          <div><b>Side panel or tab</b><p>Keep the inbox across tabs in the current Chrome window, or use the spacious dashboard.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <video src="/media/short-memory.mp4" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" aria-label="Choosing a short mailbox lifetime in Anonymail settings"></video>
          <div><b>Matched memory</b><p>Choose 10 minutes, 1 hour, 6 hours, 24 hours, or until deleted. Signup passwords match that mailbox lifetime while staying session-only.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="install" class="install-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="tutorial-intro">
          <p class="kicker light"><span></span> Installation tutorial</p>
          <h2>Install Anonymail in Developer Mode.</h2>
          <p>Follow this short video to load the free Chrome beta.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tutorial-player">
          <iframe src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/ucaRQlQ_Ojg?rel=0" title="How to install the Anonymail Developer Mode beta" loading="lazy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe>
        </div>
        <div class="tutorial-actions"><p>Watch the tutorial, download the latest beta ZIP, then choose <strong>Load unpacked</strong>.</p><a class="button inverse" href={downloadHref} download>Download latest beta</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="privacy-section wrap">
      <div><p class="kicker"><span></span> Privacy promise</p><h2>Your browsing stays in your browser.</h2></div>
      <div><p>Anonymail does not collect analytics, browsing history, signup URLs, or form contents. Mailbox operations go directly from the extension to Mail.tm.</p><a href="/privacy">Read the plain-English privacy policy →</a></div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="wrap"><a class="logo" href="/"><img src="/anonymail.png" alt="" /><span>Anonymail</span></a><p>Private signups, quietly handled.</p><div><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="https://mail.tm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Mail.tm</a></div></footer>
</BaseLayout>
